3. Commercial offerings require prior written permission

A "Commercial Offering" is any product or service made available to third
parties for a fee, subscription, advertising revenue or other commercial
consideration that distributes, embeds, bundles, hosts or exposes the Software,
a modified version, or its functionality as part of that offering. This includes:

  a. Selling, renting or commercially sublicensing copies or modified versions.
  b. Including the Software in a commercial application, plugin, appliance,
     distribution or other product, even if the Software itself is a free item.
  c. Providing a hosted service, SaaS, API or managed service through which
     customers access the Software's functionality.
  d. White-label or rebranded versions, and free tiers, trials, promotional
     bundles or loss leaders of any such Commercial Offering.

You must obtain the Owner's express written permission BEFORE making a
Commercial Offering. Public source availability, a public fork, attribution,
silence, a pull-request merge or an optional donation is not that permission.
Permission applies only to the persons, rights and scope it expressly identifies
and only to rights the Owner is entitled to grant. This license does not set a
commercial license price or require the Owner to charge for permission.

Ordinary products, code and deliverables You create with the Software do not
become Commercial Offerings merely because You used CodeBudget during their
development. This exclusion does not permit embedding or supplying the Software
or its functionality as part of those deliverables. Separate advice or training
that does not supply or host the Software is not a Commercial Offering under
this license. Voluntary donations that grant no access, feature or service
entitlement do not by themselves make a free community fork commercial.

